🪨 BLOCK 1 — PHYSICAL TOPOLOGY FAILURE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
On Michael's Samsung device, both assisted straight placement and custom-waypoint
placement reached a save review showing plausible proposed region geometry. Saving then
failed with:

"Combined dividers do not create valid planning regions"

The save-dialog presentation was also obstructed by the still-visible placement-guidance
banner and system toast. This is a failed physical-glass result. It does not grant field
acceptance or production authority.

🪨 BLOCK 2 — FORAGE-REGION PRODUCT GAP
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Michael identified that a grazing-stick observation taken for one temporary paddock must
not silently calculate total forage against the complete parent pasture. The current
implementation snapshots the parent PastureEntity acreage, so a measurement intended for
one region of a divided 140-acre pasture would still use approximately 140 acres.

Required product decision before implementation:
- allow Record Forage to target the whole parent pasture or one named active planning
  region;
- visibly show the selected acreage basis before Save;
- snapshot the selected region identity, label, geometry lineage, and acreage so later
  plan edits do not rewrite historical observations; and
- define behavior when the selected planning region is later renamed, reshaped, archived,
  deleted, or permanently converted.

This captured requirement is not silently added to ratified RW-TX-017-MPO Revision 2.
It requires an explicit corrective proposal and Michael's ratification before its data
model and archive consequences are implemented.

